Classic Worlds 2 and 3 candidate reconstructions, not authenticated original maps.

Frozen 20927-1 and 84542-1 Perlin layers were exported twice under Ruffle from Amit J Patel's
legacy demo, https://theory.stanford.edu/~amitp/_test/mapgen2-13.swf, linked in
https://simblob.blogspot.com/2012/02/polygon-map-generation-faq.html.
world02.json and world03.json pin byte hashes, x-major orientation, emulator and source identity.
The executable's exact source revision is unverified. No exporter, source dump,
client dump, sprites or historical catalogue image is bundled here.

Source/rights review: Map generation project, Copyright 2010 Amit J Patel,
MIT notice retained in MAPGEN2-LICENSE. The arrays are generated numeric output;
this notice does not relicense any third-party game content or claim permission
for the selected client's assets. WMAP references the existing selected-client
names/IDs; only the project's existing scenery palette is reused.

classic-v1 uses direct byte elevation boundaries 51/153/204 and moisture
boundaries 3/7, 4/7, 5/7, not a private-server height curve. Largest four-neighbor non-ocean mainland is retained (lakes/channels do not
split it); detached islands/coasts become empty ocean. This is a calibrated
reconstruction policy, not recovered official processing. Mainland exported coast,
roads, bridges, rivers and lakes are retained. Wet lowlands within eight tiles
of coast use ShorePlains. Generic demo lava becomes shallow water, ice becomes
lake water, snow becomes Snowy Rock: no new damaging/freezing ground.
Scenery/configuration is deterministic reconstruction, not recovered placement.
Catalogue coastline/road/lake/Godlands alignment is approximate: island outlines,
polygon detail, snow extent, historical structures and unverified variant remain
unresolved.

Rebuild offline from checkout data (no client, game state or exporter required):
  openrotmg build-realm --data data --id classic-world-02-reconstruction
  openrotmg build-realm --data data --id classic-world-02-reconstruction --check
  openrotmg build-realm --data data --id classic-world-03-reconstruction
  openrotmg build-realm --data data --id classic-world-03-reconstruction --check
